WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

This licence covers the code and documentation in this repository only.

It does NOT cover, and this repository does not distribute:

  ICRP Publication 145 phantom data
      Copyright 2020 ICRP, published by SAGE. All rights reserved. The mesh,
      the organ tables and the media compositions must be obtained from ICRP.
      See REQUIREMENTS.md. Republishing any part of that publication requires
      written permission from ICRP (annals@icrp.org).

  FLUKA, and anything compiled against it
      CERN single-user licence: personal, non-transferable, non-military,
      non-commercial, and not redistributable. Obtain your own copy from
      https://fluka.cern/download. This includes the source routine used for
      the internal-exposure case, which is CERN's own file shipped with FLUKA,
      and any executable built from it.

  Geant4, MCNP6 and PHITS reference results
      Distributed by ICRP with Publication 145, under the same terms as the
      publication. They are read from the archive you download; no copy of
      them is held here.

Note that FLUKA's own licence is itself non-commercial, so a commercial user
would in any case need to arrange terms with CERN as well as with the copyright
holder here.

